# An undo around a pasted-text block: `look` and a space typed, 1001 `x`s
# pasted (a block), Backspace takes the block and Ctrl-_ (undo) twice finds
# nothing to take back. Then 1001 `x`s pasted again, Ctrl-U kills the line
# with its block, Ctrl-Y yanks it back, and Ctrl-_ twice: the first takes the
# yank back, the second finds nothing. Ten seconds to start: on a loaded
# host a keystroke sent sooner reaches the shell instead.
wait 10
type look
key Space
pastex 1001
wait 3
snap pasted
key BSpace
wait 0.5
snap deleted
key C-_
wait 0.5
key C-_
wait 0.5
snap undone
pastex 1001
wait 3
snap pasted-again
key C-u
wait 0.5
snap killed
key C-y
wait 1
snap yanked
key C-_
wait 0.5
snap yank-undone
key C-_
wait 0.5
snap undone-again
